{
	title: "Claude's own web_search tool",
	spec: 'Requests to Anthropic Claude models include Anthropic\'s server-side web_search tool (type web_search_20250305 or the newest, max_uses 5), so Claude searches the web itself; other providers do not get it and use the google tool (task g6). The stream\'s server_tool_use and web_search_tool_result blocks are kept in history as provider-specific blocks and replayed only to Anthropic, in order and paired: an unpaired one (an interrupted turn, a compaction boundary) is dropped on replay so the API never sees half a pair. Clients show a search as a tool row: "web_search <query>" with the result titles and URLs; its cost counts in usage. A round Anthropic ends with pause_turn (a long server-side search) is not the turn's end: the turn runs another round, replaying the answer so far, and Claude goes on from it. A setting webSearch (config.ason, default true) turns it off. Artifact: the old Hal anthropic.ts web_search handling (reference, tasks/9m/old-anthropic-web-search.ts). Tests with the fake Anthropic server: the tool is offered to Claude only; paired blocks replay; an orphan is dropped; the setting turns it off; a paused round continues in the same turn.',
	status: 'done',
	needs: ['ya'],
	notes: [
		'Anthropic searches are two assistant blocks: web_search_use (server_tool_use with streamed input) and web_search_result (opaque result content). Keep their order in history and filter unpaired IDs per assistant message when building Anthropic input; other providers omit both. The transcript maps them to an ordinary tool row and a title/URL result row. webSearch is a validated boolean setting, default true, read when each request is built.'
	]
}
